course: dictionary
lesson: 7568
title: Present: a gift, here, or now
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Present has more than one meaning, so the words around it tell you which one you need. «Gran hands Sam a present.» Gran is handing something over, so present means a gift, something you give someone, often on a birthday.
explain: «A good secret, like a surprise party or a hidden present, ends happily.» Here present is a thing that could be hidden, so it is a gift again. Now try a different sentence: «Mia wants to be present in class every day.» Present means here, not absent, because she is in the room.
explain: Present can also mean now, this time, as in «at present» or «for the present». Check by swapping in now: «At now, the class is reading a book» does not sound right, so use «At present», which means right now. Always swap your meaning into the sentence to check it.
fact: «Present» can mean a gift, being here, or now. The sentence tells you which.
fact: «Present» means being here, as in «present in class». Its opposite is absent.
fact: «Present tense» is the grammar tense that tells about now, as in «I walk».
fact: «To present» means to give something formally, or to show and talk about something to a group, like a class project. It is said pre-ZENT.
fact: Phrases such as «at present», «present-day» and «for the present» all point to now.
exercise: «Gran hands Sam a present, and Sam says, "Thanks, Gran."» What is the present in this sentence? | Showing something to a group | The time right now | Being here in the room | *A gift you give someone
exercise: «Mia wants to be present in class every day.» What does present mean here? | To show a project to others | *Here, not absent | The time right now | A birthday gift
exercise: «At present, the class is reading a book.» What does at present mean? | A birthday gift | *Right now | Tomorrow morning | Long ago
test: In grammar, «I walk» is written in which tense? | Perfect tense | Past tense | Future tense | *Present tense
test: Jamal will present his project to the class on Monday. What is he going to do? | Hide it in his bag | *Show it and talk about it to the group | Throw it away | Wrap it up as a gift
exam: «A good secret, like a surprise party or a hidden present, ends happily.» In this sentence, present means | Now | To give something formally | Being here | *A gift
